Preconditions:
[PRE:SIGNIN_AS:LOYALTY_VIP_USER]
[PRE:RESET_CART]
@td(MSN_PERSKU_ALL.name) visible. Came from account dashboard (so Back has a real prior page to return to, not the browser's own history boundary).

Assertions:
[NAV] Back lands on {{FRONT_URL}}/account (the page visited before missions), not a broken or blank intermediate state {SPEC}
[STATE] the cart still holds the line written by the modal — the committed mutation is not rolled back by a client-side history navigation {BL}
[NAV] navigating forward again from {{FRONT_URL}}/account back to /account/missions renders the page fresh, with no resurrected stale modal open {SPEC}

[DOM] a graceful re-authentication prompt or a redirect to sign-in is visible, and the raw unhandled 401, a blank white page, and a permanently spinning modal are all absent {BL}
[DOM] no raw GraphQL error object, stack frame or HTTP status code is visible to the customer {BL}
[NAV] after re-authenticating, the customer lands back on /account/missions rather than a generic dashboard, matching MSNF-003's established returnUrl contract for this route {SPEC}

[DOM] the missions page's own heading and its mission card grid are both visible despite the corrupted cart cache, and the points-balance banner (a separate, cart-independent data source) is also visible — a cart-storage fault must not blank an unrelated page region {BL}
[DOM] the modal either opens cleanly (self-healing by refetching cart state from the server rather than trusting the corrupted cache) or fails with a scoped, customer-readable error — a full white screen or an unhandled exception is absent in either case {BL}
[STATE] if the add-to-cart write is attempted, it either succeeds and the cart-cache is repaired to a valid state, or it fails visibly — a write that silently succeeds server-side while the client cache stays corrupted, so the header count is now wrong, is the specific failure this case exists to catch {HYPOTHESIS}
[REL] if the add-to-cart write is attempted and succeeds, the header cart indicator value = the cart page's own total unit count afterward — a self-consistency check that the corrupted cache did not leave the client showing a stale count while the server holds a different one {BL}
